# =============================================================================
# Environment variables — TEMPLATE (safe to commit)
# =============================================================================
# Rules (.ai/SECURITY.md):
#   - This file documents variable NAMES and placeholders ONLY. Never real values.
#   - Copy to `.env` locally and fill in real values there. `.env*` is gitignored.
#   - Client-exposed variables must use your framework's public prefix and
#     contain nothing sensitive — anything shipped to the browser is public.
#   - Read env vars only through the single typed config module
#     (.ai/ARCHITECTURE.md → Configuration).
#
# Replace the examples below with your project's real variable names at setup
# (.ai/TEMPLATE-SETUP.md §5) and keep this file in sync with every release.
# =============================================================================

# --- App ---
# NODE_ENV=development
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Database ---
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME

# --- Auth (example: managed provider) ---
# AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-generated-secret
# AUTH_PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
# AUTH_PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-me

# --- External services (one block per service, note where the key comes from) ---
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace-me        # Stripe dashboard → Developers → API keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace-me                # transactional email
